menu "AIWatchOS OS"

config AIWATCHOS_DISPLAY_SLEEP_TIMEOUT_S
    int "Display inactivity sleep timeout (seconds)"
    default 30
    range 0 3600
    help
        Seconds without touch or button input before the CO5300 panel is
        put to sleep (display off + SLPIN) and the main loop pauses all
        rendering. Wake is on touch, BOOT, or PWR press; the touch that
        wakes the panel is swallowed so it cannot fire the UI element
        under it. Set to 0 to disable the inactivity timeout (the PWR
        short-press sleep/wake toggle still works).

config AIWATCHOS_TZ_OFFSET_MIN
    int "Displayed time-of-day offset from UTC (minutes)"
    default -240
    range -720 840
    help
        Offset applied ONLY when deriving the displayed time-of-day
        (status bar + clock face) from the UTC epoch. Default -240 =
        EDT (UTC-4). The epoch itself stays true UTC everywhere else:
        the PCF85063 RTC, SNTP discipline and all protocols keep UTC.

endmenu
